<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Arrapha</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1340 BCE (approx.) · capital Arrapha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Hurrian kingdom around modern Kirkuk, vassal of Mitanni, whose town of Nuzi left thousands of tablets on family life, land and law.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Arrapha, the ancient name of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kirkuk">Kirkuk</a>, became the capital of a Hurrian kingdom east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> in the 15th century BCE, when the region fell within the sphere of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire</a>. Its kings ruled the plain between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-zab">Lesser Zab</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> foothills as Mitannian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The best evidence comes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuzi">Nuzi</a> (Yorghan Tepe), a provincial town excavated in the 1920s and 1930s, where over 5,000 tablets were found. Written in a local Akkadian with many Hurrian words, they record family archives such as that of Tehip-tilla, adoptions used to transfer land, slave contracts, marriage settlements and lawsuits. Society was dominated by the palace and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a>-owning families. Kings such as Kipi-Teshup and Ithi-Teshup are named in seal impressions and documents.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> weakened in the mid-14th century BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuzi">Nuzi</a> was burnt around 1340 BCE, probably by Assyrian forces, and Arrapha was soon absorbed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>, later becoming an Assyrian province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-arrapha.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Arrapha" width="320" height="333"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meso2mil-English.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1340 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Arrapha</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kipi-Teshup, Ithi-Teshup</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hurrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hurrian, Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Arrapha, Arrapkha, Arraphe</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1420&amp;focus=kingdom-of-arrapha" aria-label="Kingdom of Arrapha on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5802 896 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Arrapha lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6122 1152L5996 1079M6122 1152L6092 1134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5996 1079h0M6092 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6122 1152h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6122 1152h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-1420&amp;focus=kingdom-of-arrapha">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

